Article 28-2 (Person in charge of derivatives business) (1) A financial investment business entity prescribed by Presidential Decree, taking into account the size of assets, types of financial investment business, etc. (including a concurrently-run financial investment entity) shall appoint at least one person to take charge of derivatives business prescribed by Presidential Decree as a full-time executive officer (including persons referred to in the subparagraphs of Article 401-2(1) of the Commercial Act). <Amended on Jul. 31, 2015; Mar. 29, 2016>
