Article 447 (Concurrent imposition of imprisonment with labor and fine) (1) Where any person is punished by imprisonment with labor under Article 443(1) or (2), the fine prescribed in Article 443(1) (excluding subparagraph 10) and (2) shall be imposed concurrently. <Added on Dec. 30, 2014; Jan. 5, 2021>
  (2) Any person who commits a crime under any provision of Articles 443(1)10 and 444 through 446 may be punished by imprisonment with labor and a fine concurrently. <Amended on Dec. 30, 2014; Jan. 5, 2021>

Article 447-2 (Confiscation and additional collection) (1) The property acquired by a person who falls under any subparagraph of Article 443(1) (excluding subparagraph 10) shall be confiscated, and if confiscation is unfeasible, the value thereof shall be collected punitively. <Amended on Jan. 5, 2021; Jun. 8, 2021>
  (2) The property that a person who falls under any of Article 443(1)4 through 7 has provided or intends to provide for the relevant activity shall be confiscated, and if it is impossible to confiscate it, the value equivalent thereto shall be collected. <Added on Jun. 8, 2021>
  [This Article Added on Dec. 30, 2014]

Article 448 (Joint penalty provisions) If the representative of a corporation (including an organization; hereafter in this Article the same shall apply) or an agent, employee of, or other persons employed by, the corporation or an individual commits any violation prescribed in Articles 443 through 446 in connection with the business of the corporation or the individual, not only shall such offender be punished accordingly, but the corporation or the individual shall be punished by a fine under the relevant Articles; provided, this shall not apply where such corporation or individual has not been negligent in giving due attention and supervision over the relevant business to prevent such violation.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Feb. 3, 2009]

Article 448-2 (Reduction or exemption of punishment) (1) A person who violates Article 173-2(2), 174, 176, or 178 surrenders himself or herself to an investigative agency (including cases where he or she voluntarily reports to the Securities and Futures Commission; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article), or conducts an investigation or trial; Where a person is punished for his or her own crime in connection with a statement or testimony that reveals another person's crime in the relevant case, the submission of other materials, or information for the arrest of an offender, the punishment may be mitigated or exempted.
  (2) The Financial Services Commission shall, in connection with an act of surrendering himself or herself pursuant to paragraph (1), a statement or testimony that reveals another person's crime with respect to the relevant case, submission of other materials, or information for arresting an offender, shall be deemed a violation under Article 429-2. Any person on whom a penalty surcharge has been imposed under paragraph (1) may be reduced or exempted from the penalty surcharge.
  (3) Detailed matters concerning the scope of persons subject to reduction or exemption of penalty surcharges pursuant to paragraph (2) and the criteria and degree of reduction or exemption shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.
  [This Article Added on Jul. 18, 2023]

