ADDENDA <Act No. 18128, Apr. 20, 2021>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Applicability concerning duty to deliver explanatory statements at investment recommendations for general private equity funds)
The amended provisions of Article 249-4(2) through (7) shall begin to apply from the first issue of an explanation after this Act enters into force.
Article 3 (Applicability to audits of general private equity funds)
The amended provisions of Article 249-8(2)4 shall begin to apply from the last day of the fiscal year in which this Act enters into force or from the date on which any ground specified in Article 240(3) arises after this Act enters into force.
Article 4 (Applicability concerning special purpose company)
The amended provisions of Article 249-13(6) shall apply from a special-purpose company established after this Act enters into force.
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning hedge fund business)
A person who engages in hedge fund investment business as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed to have completed the registration of general private equity fund business in accordance with the amended provisions of Article 249-3.
Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning hedge funds)
(1) A hedge fund established and reported under the former Article 249-6 before this Act enters into force shall be deemed a general private equity fund established and reported pursuant to the amended provisions of Article 249-6.
(2) Among the collective investment property managed by a hedge fund under paragraph (1), any investment falling under the amended provisions of Article 249-7(5)1 as of the date this Act enters into force shall be deemed to fall thereunder on from the date this Act enters into force.
Article 7 (Transitional measures concerning deferment of redemption of general private equity funds)
The amended provisions of the proviso of Article 249-8(5) shall not apply where any cause for postponement of redemption occurs before this Act enters into force.
Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning private equity fund)
(1) A private equity fund established and reported under the former Article 249-10 before this Act enters into force and a special-purpose company in which such private equity fund has invested as a shareholder or partner under the former Article 249-13(1)3a shall be deemed an institutional private equity fund established and established and reported pursuant to the amended provisions of Article 249-10 and a special-purpose company invested by the institutional private equity as a shareholder or partner thereof.
(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the former provisions of Articles 249-12 and 249-13 shall apply where there is any executive officer or employee is not provided for in the amended provisions of Article 249-11(6) among a private equity fund established and reported under the former Article 249-10 before this Act enters into force and a special purpose company in which the private equity fund has invested as shareholders or partners under the former Article 249-13(1)3a, which is a special purpose company for its management.
(3) A private equity fund for corporate financial stability established and reported pursuant to the former Article 249-22 and a special purpose company in which the private equity fund invested as shareholder or partner pursuant to paragraph (3) of the same Article before this Act enters into force shall be deemed a private equity fund for corporate financial stability and established and reported pursuant to the amended provisions of Article 249-22 and a special purpose company in which the private equity fund invested as shareholder or partner.
(4) A private equity fund for start-up and venture business established and reported pursuant to the former Article 249-23 and a special purpose company in which the private equity fund invested as shareholder or partner pursuant to paragraph (3) of the same Article before this Act enters into force shall be deemed a private equity fund for start-up and venture business and established and reported pursuant to the amended provisions of Article 249-23 and a special purpose company in which the private equity fund invested as shareholder or partner.
(5) No private equity fund, private equity fund for corporate financial stability, or private equity fund for start-up or venture business under paragraphs (1) through (4) may obtain any additional investment agreement as from the enforcement date of this Act; provided, excluded here from shall be investment agreements made by investors under the amended provisions of Article 249-11(6)1.
(6) A private equity fund for corporate financial stability, the private equity fund for start-up and venture business, and a special purpose company in which they invested as shareholders or partners under paragraphs (1) through (4) shall dispose equity securities under subparagraph 1 or 2 of the same paragraph to a third person within 15 years from the date of acquisition of the relevant equity securities in applying the amended provisions of Article 249-7(5) applied mutatis mutandis in the amended provisions of Article 249-12.
Article 9 (Transitional measures concerning managing members of private equity funds)
(1) A managing member of a private equity fund registered as at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed a managing member registered under the amended provisions of Article 249-15.
(2) Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 249-15(1)3, the managing members of a private equity fund registered as at the time this Act enters into force shall be governed by the former provisions until one year passes from the date this Act enters into force.
Article 10 Omitted.

